.TH starforge-orchestrate 1  StarForge "User Manual"
.SH NAME
starforge\-orchestrate \- Multi\-contract deployment orchestration
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstarforge\-orchestrate\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Multi\-contract deployment orchestration
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH EXECUTE OPTIONS
.TP
\fBstarforge orchestrate execute --file <manifest.json> [--dry-run]\fR
Build the plan and execute it sequentially (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-concurrency <N>\fR
Deploy independent contracts in parallel with up to <N> worker threads.
Dependency order is preserved: contracts sharing a dependency depth form a
wave, and waves run in strict order. Use \fBauto\fR to size the pool from the
host's parallel CPU count (capped at 8).
.SH PROPAGATION
Parallel deployment issues contract uploads across independent deployment
steps within each wave; checkpoint state is persisted after every step, so
resume/rollback guarantees are identical to sequential execution.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
